        "id": 12756,
        "name": "HRM",
        "username": "HRM",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/d9b06d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-29T17:43:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>OK, so I'm not exactly certain which forum to post this in, so I'll try here.It's not exactly a rules question, but more of a... Desgin question, or strategy question, maybe?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So I played in Silver Gulch for the first time last night, and stumbled across something I couldn't quite grasp the point of. The text on \"Sustain The Portal\" allows one player to discard a card, allowing you to then discard the top card of the Environment deck. But the damage it does after that isn't preventable, so... Like, why would you bother? I'm assuming there's some interaction here that I'm missing, but I don't see it. Like, I guess if I were playing Haka and wanted to destroy Environment cards, then sure. But otherwise, I kinda... Don't get it?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Can someone school me on this? Thanks!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:22.727Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 12754,
        "topic_slug": "curious-about-sustain-the-portal",
        "display_username": "HRM",
        "primary_group_name": null,
