        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>OK, so I&#39;m not exactly certain which forum to post this in, so I&#39;ll try here.It&#39;s not exactly a rules question, but more of a... Desgin question, or strategy question, maybe?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So I played in Silver Gulch for the first time last night, and stumbled across something I couldn&#39;t quite grasp the point of. The text on &quot;Sustain The Portal&quot; allows one player to discard a card, allowing you to then discard the top card of the Environment deck. But the damage it does after that isn&#39;t preventable, so... Like, why would you bother? I&#39;m assuming there&#39;s some interaction here that I&#39;m missing, but I don&#39;t see it. Like, I guess if I were playing Haka and wanted to destroy Environment cards, then sure. But otherwise, I kinda... Don&#39;t get it?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Can someone school me on this? Thanks!</p>",
